To fix the CORS error, add the following to your Express server before your routes:

```js
const cors = require('cors');
app.use(cors({ origin: 'http://localhost:5173' }));
```

Then restart the server and refresh the page. If you still see the error, open the Network tab and check the response headers for `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`. You can also copy that header output and paste it here and I'll take a look. Remember to restrict the origin in production instead of allowing all.
